course: dictionary
lesson: 13499
title: Imaginative
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Someone who is imaginative is good at thinking of new, clever or creative ideas. «Maya's imaginative story had a dragon who baked cakes for the whole village.» Dragons do not really bake cakes, so Maya made the idea up. That is what imaginative means: creative and full of new ideas.
explain: Use the words around the word to check its meaning. «Sam built an imaginative den out of old boxes, sheets and string.» The words new and creative are not in the sentence, but building a den from old boxes shows Sam had clever ideas. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «Sam built a creative den» still make sense? It does, so you are right.
explain: Imaginative is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a story, an idea or a person. It can change: more imaginative, most imaginative. «Her drawings are more imaginative than mine» means her drawings have more new and creative ideas than yours.
fact: Imaginative means good at thinking of new, clever or creative ideas.
fact: «An imaginative story» means a story full of creative ideas.
fact: Imaginative comes from the word imagine, which means to picture or create something in your mind.
fact: «Imaginative play» is pretend play where children invent their own games, characters and worlds.
fact: Imaginative is an adjective: imaginative, more imaginative, most imaginative.
exercise: «The inventor's imaginative machine could turn rain into music.» What does imaginative mean here? | Exactly like every other machine | Tired and sleepy | * Full of new, creative ideas | Made of heavy metal
exercise: «The children's imaginative play turned the garden into a jungle.» Which word tells you the play used creative ideas? | * imaginative | garden | children | jungle
exercise: Priya always has ___ ideas, like painting her bedroom ceiling as a starry sky. Which word fits best? | boring | sleepy | heavy | * imaginative
test: «Tom wrote an imaginative ending where the moon talked to a fox.» What does imaginative mean here? | Hungry | Quiet | * Creative and full of new ideas | Dark and cold
test: Which word means the same as imaginative? | Sleepy | * Creative | Boring | Careful
exam: Which phrase best describes a child who invents a secret language and a map of an imaginary island? | * Highly imaginative | Lazy and bored | Very hungry | Quite noisy
